  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI've got 3 workers set up for my synapse instance, a synchrotron, a federation sender, and a federation reader. All 3 will go down for a few minutes every so often. I haven't figured out how to reproduce this but it does happen very often. I've got a log attached, browsing through it I don't see any actual cause for the problems but there's a lot of weird stuff going on with the workers pausing and resuming a bunch of times in there. Also according to the logs the federation reader I think completely stops anything happening on the server for 3 minutes.\r\n\r\n[syn_log.txt](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/files/5224309/syn_log.txt)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Wait for 20 minutes or so and you'll see it\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: please answer the following questions, to help us narrow down the problem -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Was this issue identified on matrix.org or another homeserver? -->\r\n- **Homeserver**: riot.firechicken.net\r\n\r\nIf not matrix.org:\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n What version of Synapse is running?\r\n\r\nYou can find the Synapse version with this command:\r\n\r\n$ curl http://localhost:8008/_synapse/admin/v1/server_version\r\n\r\n(You may need to replace `localhost:8008` if Synapse is not configured to\r\nlisten on that port.)\r\n-->\r\n- **Version**: 1.19.1\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: pip\r\n<!-- examples: package manager/git clone/pip  -->\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: CentOS VPS\r\n<!--\r\nTell us about the environment in which your homeserver is operating\r\ndistro, hardware, if it's running in a vm/container, etc.\r\n-->\r\n",
